# {{agent_name}}

> Generated by [meta-agent](https://github.com/albertfolch-renal/meta-agent)

## Quick Start

1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in your API keys:
   ```bash
   cp .env.example .env
   ```

2. Install dependencies:
   ```bash
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```

3. Run in development mode:
   ```bash
   python run_adk.py
   ```

## Project Structure

```
{{agent_package}}/
  agent.py          # Root agent definition
  config/           # LLM and logging configuration
  plugins/          # Plugin chain (trace, cache, resilience, etc.)
  prompt/           # System prompt and instruction builder
  tools/            # Custom tool definitions
  skills/           # Skill directories (auto-discovered)
  contexts/         # Domain knowledge .md files (loaded into prompt)
  state/            # Session state and caching
  utils/            # Shared utilities (resilience, date, etc.)
  callbacks/        # Custom callback handlers
```

## Adding Tools

Edit `{{agent_package}}/tools/__init__.py` and add your tool functions to the `get_tools()` return list.

## Adding Skills

Create a subdirectory under `{{agent_package}}/skills/` with a `SKILL.md` file. Skills are auto-discovered at startup.

## Adding Domain Knowledge

Place `.md` files in `{{agent_package}}/contexts/`. They are loaded into the agent's system prompt automatically.

## Configuration

See `.env.example` for all available environment variables.
